From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Bienvenu <davidbienvenu@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:18:07 -0700
Subject: Ensure dragend event sent when drag aborted in StartDragging()

For the case where a user is doing very fast clicks on draggable items,
the item may start a drag, but then we find the mouse is no longer down.
In this case, we must send a dragend event.

We call EndDrag() rather than ClearDragStateOnStartFailure() which can
be removed since in the other places where it is called it is sufficient
to call only SystemDragEnded().

ClearDragStateOnStartFailure() was added in crrev.com/c/8356989 to
clean up the state of `drag_security_info_`.  This CL maintains that
fix.  In the first 2 cases `drag_security_info_` is already in the
empty state when we exit, in the next 2 cases, calling EndDrag() will
clear `drag_security_info_` and also send the enddrag event.

Bug: 522564418
